THE KEOGH PLAN AGREEMENT

This Keogh Plan Agreement (the "Agreement") is entered into as of January 1, 2022 (the "Effective Date"), by and between Jane Doe, a self-employed individual (the "Participant"), and ABC Enterprises, a sole proprietorship (the "Employer").

1. Purpose. The purpose of this Agreement is to establish a Keogh Plan (the "Plan") for the exclusive benefit of the Participant and to set forth the terms and conditions upon which the Participant and the Employer will make contributions to the Plan, invest the assets of the Plan, and distribute the benefits payable under the Plan.

2. Contributions.

a. The Participant and the Employer may each make contributions to the Plan on behalf of the Participant, subject to the following limitations:

i. The total contributions made by the Participant and the Employer on behalf of the Participant for any taxable year may not exceed the lesser of (A) 25% of the Participant's earned income from the Employer for the taxable year, or (B) $58,000 for 2022 (as adjusted for cost-of-living increases in subsequent years).

ii. The Participant's contributions may not exceed 100% of the Participant's earned income from the Employer for the taxable year.

iii. The Employer's contributions may not exceed 25% of the Participant's earned income from the Employer for the taxable year.

b. Contributions must be made in cash and must be made no later than the due date (including extensions) for the filing of the Participant's federal income tax return for the taxable year to which the contributions relate.

